Z||000000||wilburt||07-01-2000||09:37 AM||||Here's the info:<P>Torque (SAE net)..........134 ft. lbs.@<BR>                            2800RPM<P>Thermostat Housing Cap....AC Type<BR>                            RC40<P>Thermostat Temp Spec......91*C (195*F)<P>Under the introduction, (your page 2), the word you can't read is 'Stoichiometric'.<P>The last paragraph in the intro section reads different than what you have. My '86 2M4 was made in the last half of the year, after there were some changes, like motor mounts, etc. so I'm thinking Pontiac put out two D-I-Y manuals, one making reference to the GT. Heres how mine reads:<P>Fiero SE and Fiero GT-Added performance and Power<P>The 1986 Pontiac Fiero continues to build excitement with the SE Coupe and the new GT Coupe. Equipped with a four-speed manual transaxle 2.8 Liter V6 engine(standard on GT), they boast 0-60 performance in 8.5 seconds. The GT features distinctive fastback styling with a new rear facia, with integral spoiler, and new quarter windows. Both SE and GT feature aerodynamic front facias and ground effect side skirts. Also standard on the GT are 205/60R15 front tires and 215/60R15 rear tires mounted on 15 inch diamond spoke aluminum wheels. The look is performance with power and sleekness giving Fiero an unbeatable combination.<P>In your specifications page 2,under GENERAL SPECIFICATIONS, all the numbers are good, but my manual reads:<P>Track(Except SE and GT)<P>Track(SE or GT)<P>Length<BR>  Except SE and GT<BR>  SE or GT<P>Under Suspension,(your same page 2),you listed the steering type instead of the suspenstion type.<P>Under Wheels, mine also list a size for the GT 15"x 6.0" aluminum.<P>Under tires, Also listed is: <BR>GT front........205/60r15 steel radial<BR>GT rear.........215/60r15 steel radial<P>Your page 3: <BR>Engine oil<BR>  6-cyl.........AC Type PF 51<BR> mine reads     AC Type PF 47<P>That's about it. I could loan you this manual if ya need it.<P>||||reg||1
